Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; What Volume Control (sndvol32) shows by default for the demo's AC'97 card. ReactOS's Volume Control shows only the lines that its
; saved choice lists, and a fresh user has none, so its window opens empty although the card has eight lines. These are the choices
; Options > Properties would save: the master volume on the Playback side, and the Microphone on the Recording side. The card's other
; lines (Aux, Video, CD Audio, Line In, Phone Line and PC Speaker, and the microphone's playback monitor) connect to nothing in the
; virtual card, so they stay hidden, which is what the Volume Control does with a line it has no choice for. Each value is a list of
; records: a DWORD of flags (0 shows the line, 4 hides it) and the line's name as 64 UTF-16 characters. The key names are the mixer's
; product name and the destination line's name.
